= The Reparation Question


About since the murder of <span style="color: [+ ddp_colour +];">**Rathenau**</span> Germany's already dangerous inflation has skyrocketed. Meanwhile tons of coal and timber are shipped to the Western Allies as reparation payments. So far the government has tried to show the impossibility of fulfilling the demands by trying to fulfill them - a heavily criticised policy by many voices from about all directions.

Yet not all hope is lost, the British government has shown itself willing to lower the reparation demands seeing the initial ammount mostly as an internal propaganda win - though the French government still needs to be convinced of that approach.

- @deal_questionmark

@deal_questionmark
title: Can we settle the matter?
subtitle: We should at least arrange a plan to stabilize our currency and reduce the payments.


Raymond Poincaré, primer-minister of France, opposes any deal that will mess with Versailles.

- @menu_for_december_1922: What should we do next?

